{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>נכתה.</b> A plural form, like ויהי ידיו אמונה, ועיניו קמה, בנות צעדה." "<b>For the flax was באביב (in bloom).</b> The reason Scripture did not join flax and barley under the term אביב as it joined wheat and spelt under אפילות is that flax, whether sown early or sown late, is always a stalk — unlike other plants. Therefore הפשתה is written separately. But wheat and spelt, if sown together, grow in the same manner." "<b>והפשתה גבעל.</b> This implies that if it had not been a stalk it would not have been struck. This is difficult, for it is written: ואת כל עשב השדה הכה הברד."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:47.157216336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}